 "deepDive": {
  "domain": "Technology, AI & cyber",
  "title": "The week the plumbing showed: e-government, chips and AI rules",
  "body": "**Poland’s digital front door went dark.** ePUAP is how Poles file official requests, sign documents with a Trusted Profile and receive letters from offices. On Tuesday evening the digital minister said an attack had been detected and stopped, and the platform was pulled offline as a precaution ([Wirtualnemedia](https://www.wirtualnemedia.pl/atak-hakerzy-epuap-system-dane-osobowe-polakow-minister-cyfryzacji-krzysztof-gawkowski-zawiadomi-abw,7349814817622496a)). The ministry insists nothing was compromised, but it gave no return date, and the ABW is investigating. No one has been blamed yet. The incident adds to a run of attacks on Polish public systems and lands as the government pushes a data-protection law after a breach of 19 million people’s records.\n\n**In the US, Nvidia is both a company and a policy tool.** Its chips sit at the centre of export controls on China. The board is reportedly close to removing Jensen Huang after he admitted a relationship with a woman US intelligence reportedly saw as gathering information for China ([SF Standard](https://sfstandard.com/2026/11/11/jensen-huang-reportedly-fired-nvidia-board-affair-direct-report-alleged/)). Separately, Reuters records suggest restricted H200 chips still reach blacklisted Chinese military universities through resellers. Both stories feed congressional pressure on export licensing, a week before Trump and Xi are due to meet around APEC in Shenzhen, where a new US–China AI dialogue is to begin.\n\n**Europe and India are writing the rulebooks.** A new Commission regulation sets common rules for AI sandboxes, the supervised testbeds Poland must offer under the AI Act. India’s data-protection rules reach a new stage tomorrow, when consent-manager provisions take effect, and a MeitY consultation on AI safety and deepfakes is expected within days.\n\n**What to watch:** when ePUAP comes back and whether attribution follows; Nvidia’s board decision; and whether Shenzhen produces anything concrete on AI.",
  "links": [
   {
    "label": "Wirtualnemedia",
    "url": "https://www.wirtualnemedia.pl/atak-hakerzy-epuap-system-dane-osobowe-polakow-minister-cyfryzacji-krzysztof-gawkowski-zawiadomi-abw,7349814817622496a"
   },
   {
    "label": "SF Standard",
    "url": "https://sfstandard.com/2026/11/11/jensen-huang-reportedly-fired-nvidia-board-affair-direct-report-alleged/"
   },
   {
    "label": "AI Weekly",
    "url": "https://aiweekly.co/ai-news-today"
   }
  ]
 },
